The systematic due to the uncertainty of the BEMC tower energy scale is found in the exact same way as the track \(p_{T}\) systematic. The tower energy was scaled up and down by 3.7% before the jet finder was run. The value of 3.7% is the estimated uncertainty in the average absolute gain of the BEMC towers (see discussion in appendix A). Figure 5.7 shows the size of the BEMC tower energy systematic.

