Section 5.1 described how di-jets were sorted into the L2JetHigh and JP1 trigger samples based on the properties of the individual jets in the di-jet. The L2JetHigh sample contains many more events than the JP1 sample, as can be seen in figure 5.14, and so combining JP1 with L2JetHigh would not significantly reduce the statistical errors, compared to using the L2JetHigh sample alone. Because of this, only the L2JetHigh sample was used for the final cross section result.

